spec:
  grid: 18-30 rows x 18-30 cols, always square [observed]
  background: 0
  major_foreground: color 1; forms all network structure
  components:
    count: 2-3 disjoint 4-connected networks; Chebyshev separation >= 2
    each_has: exactly 1 singleton marker pixel in a unique non-{0,1} color
    marker_position: always in a thick interior cell (full 3x3 neighborhood inside component)
    marker_colors: all distinct within grid; drawn from {2,3,4,6,8} [observed]
    no_endpoints: every pixel has >= 2 same-component 4-neighbors (no dead ends)
  network_structure: |
    Each network = several solid rectangular blocks (3-7 rows x 3-12 cols)
    connected by width-1 axis-aligned corridors (length 1-6 cells).
    Blocks per component: 2-9. Corridors per component: 1-8.
  foreground_density: 31-47% of grid
  interior_ratio: 10-42% of each component's pixels have full 3x3 support
  transform:
    for each component, every pixel whose full 3x3 neighborhood is inside
    the same component gets recolored to that component's marker color;
    all other pixels (borders, corridors, background) stay unchanged

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct construction (blocks + corridors)
  steps:
    1. Choose grid size N x N (18-30).
    2. Decide number of components K (2-3).
    3. For each component, place 2-9 solid rectangular blocks (>=3x3) of color 1
       on the grid without overlapping other components. Ensure Chebyshev gap >= 2
       between components.
    4. Connect blocks within each component via width-1 corridors of color 1
       (horizontal or vertical, length 1-6). Corridors exit from block edges.
       Ensure the component is 4-connected and has no dead-end pixels.
    5. Place one marker pixel (unique non-{0,1} color) inside each component
       at a cell with full 3x3 support (all 8 neighbors in same component).
    6. Validate: each component is 4-connected, no endpoints, marker is in
       thick interior, foreground density 30-50%.
